FILE: app/src/skip-to-end.ts
```ts
import type { AnimationGroup } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import { pauseAnimation } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function skipToEnd(group: AnimationGroup): void {
    group.currentTime = group.duration;
    group._evaluate?.();
    pauseAnimation(group);
}
```

I set `currentTime` to `duration` so the progress bar reads 100%, called the group's `_evaluate` to write the final keyframe values into the model so it displays the end pose, and then called `pauseAnimation` to stop playback so the pose is held while the scene keeps rendering. The one thing I'm not fully certain of is whether `_evaluate` is always populated on a playing group (it's optional in the type); if for some reason it were undefined the pose wouldn't be forced, but since the group is stated to be playing it should be present.
